EXT. MESA OVERLOOK, HIGH DESERT - DAWN

Red rock. A sky going gold. Four riders reining in on the edge of a drop that falls a thousand feet to the canyon floor.

A man in a black duster, a STRANGER, holds his horse apart, a rifle across the saddle. The three behind him wait: CAPTAIN LEONIDAS HARGROVE-ABASI (50s, cavalry hat), a gunslinger called SALLY QUILLFEATHER-DIAZ (30s, two revolvers, one scarred cheek), and a boy bugler, OWEN TIBBS-OKORO (15).

LEONIDAS
(to the Stranger)
Your name, friend.

STRANGER
Don't have one.

SALLY
Everyone has one.

OWEN
(excited)
Maybe he's a ghost!

STRANGER
(dryly)
Maybe.

He lowers the rifle. He looks at Sally for a long moment, and something passes behind his eyes.

STRANGER (CONT'D)
Sally Quillfeather. Last time I saw you, you were nine.

SALLY
Who the hell --

STRANGER
Ephraim. Ephraim Quillfeather.

SALLY
My brother's dead.

EPHRAIM
So they told you.

LEONIDAS
(over him)
Stand down, Sally!

SALLY ^
(over him)
Don't you dare, Ephraim!

The echo rolls off the mesa and into the canyon. Owen lifts his bugle halfway to his mouth, then lowers it. Nobody moves.
